abstract: >
  IPAseek is a bioinformatics pipeline to detect intronic polyadenylation (IPA)
  sites from RNA-seq datasets. It identifies locations within gene introns where
  premature polyadenylation occurs, quantifies IPA usage across samples, and
  produces a SummarizedExperiment object for downstream analysis. The pipeline
  runs on SLURM-based HPC clusters and uses PELT changepoint detection on
  per-base genomic coverage signals to identify IPA events.
